Project Title: Simple Password Manager

Description:
Create a basic password manager using Python that securely stores and manages user passwords.
This project will involve encryption, hashing, and basic user interface implementation.


Features:
User Registration: Allow users to create an account with a master password.
Password Storage: Enable users to add, view, and delete their stored passwords.
Encryption: Encrypt the stored passwords using a secure encryption algorithm (e.g., AES).
Hashing: Hash the master password using a strong hash function (e.g., SHA-256).
User Authentication: Implement a login system to authenticate users with their master password.
Clipboard Clearing: Implement a feature that automatically clears the clipboard after a certain period to enhance security.
Generate Strong Passwords: Include an option to generate strong, random passwords for users.
Local Storage: Store the encrypted password data locally on the user's machine.
Master Password Recovery: Implement a secure master password recovery mechanism (e.g., using security questions).
GUI (Graphical User Interface): Create a simple graphical interface for users to interact with the password manager.


Libraries/Modules to Consider:
cryptography (for encryption)
hashlib (for hashing)
tkinter (for GUI)
pyperclip (for clipboard manipulation)


Security Considerations:
Use industry-standard encryption and hashing algorithms.
Ensure secure handling of the master password.
Protect against common security threats like injection attacks.

Bonus Features (Optional, if time permits):
Cloud Sync: Implement the ability to sync encrypted password data across devices (consider the security implications).
Two-Factor Authentication: Add an extra layer of security with 2FA.
Password Strength Checker: Evaluate and display the strength of user passwords.
Remember to focus on code quality, documentation, and security best practices. Good luck with your project!